U9 (Round-11): per-residue altlocs (N8) on a feature patch.

Provenance note (honest): the original N8 branch tip e9985c6 was lost
with the prior sandbox reset and is NOT restored or claimed. This is a
FRESH implementation on the science tip; commit SHAs differ from the
lost series by construction.

What it adds:
- An opt-in per_residue conformer-selection policy in
  backend/tos/ingestion/processor.py, shared by the PDB and mmCIF parse
  paths via _select_conformers(). One altloc ID per residue chosen by
  TOTAL occupancy (first-seen on ties); blank-altloc atoms are shared
  and always kept; the per-atom rule still applies within survivors.
- The DEFAULT policy stays per_atom (P0 item 6 invariant, unchanged);
  flipping the engine default changes measurement semantics and is
  owner-gated.
- backend/tests/test_altloc_per_residue.py: 12 tests (chimera
  prevention, blank-altloc retention, tie-break, no-duplicate-keys
  guarantee, mmCIF parity, default unchanged incl. the pinned 3ERD
  tie assertion).

Test evidence (this environment, commit 240d710):
- tests/test_altloc_per_residue.py + tests/test_altloc_selection.py:
  20 passed.
- Full backend suite: 4 failed / 514 passed / 5 skipped. The 4 failures
  (test_b6_regression.py::TestUsageWidget) are PRE-EXISTING at base
  ebc1fd79 in this environment — verified by running the same tests on
  the unmodified base — and are unrelated to conformer selection.

Patch only; merge is owner-gated.


